diff --git a/docs/harness/log.md b/docs/harness/log.md
index 1b09cc68d..38376ca9f 100644
--- a/docs/harness/log.md
+++ b/docs/harness/log.md
@@ -110,3 +110,11 @@ Risks seen before the harness:
 - full-gate: Left out of bin/harness check: system tests (bin/harness test-system, need Chrome and a Mermaid.js download), the Bazaar non-ASCII test (needs the en_US.ISO8859-1 locale), bundle audit (needs network), and the PostgreSQL/MySQL and Ruby 3.3/3.4 matrix. The upstream workflows tests.yml and linters.yml still run all of them.
 - ci: The uw-harness package is not published on npm (npx -y uw-harness returned 404 here), so the new harness.yml workflow will fail until it is published. The gates were checked with the local build of uw-harness (check passes) and run directly from a clean shell.
 - deploy-explicit: Without human answers, docs/deploy.md and docs/observability.md keep open TODO blocks, so these two checks stay partial.
+
+## 2026-11-02: warn when search terms of a text filter are truncated (#44464)
+
+Text filters (string, text and search types) with an operator that splits the value into search terms (`~`, `*~`, `!~`, `^`, `$`) used only the first 5 terms, and the rest was dropped silently. `Redmine::Search::Tokenizer` now has `MAX_TOKENS = 5` and `truncated?`. `Query#filter_warnings` returns one message per truncated filter. The issue list, time entries (list and report), calendar and Gantt chart show the messages as `<p class="warning">` above the results through `render_query_filter_warnings`. Warnings do not make the query invalid. Tests cover the tokenizer, the query model, the helper (escaping) and the four views. `check-fast` and `check` pass.
+
+What was learned: `$` (ends with) also splits the value into terms through `Query.tokenized_like_conditions`, so it is included with the operators listed in the issue. Only the first value of a filter is used by the SQL, so only that value is checked. The message key is `notice_query_search_terms_truncated` (next to the Gantt truncation notice). Other locales fall back to English.
+
+Left: the issues report and the search page (`/search`) do not show the warning; the search page already shows its own tokens (`@tokens`).
